        "base": "https://www.wananga.com/feed/rss2",
        "language": null,
        "type": "text/html",
        "value": "<div>\n  <h3>\n    <span>\n      <span>\n        \n            Kaik\u014dkiri \u2013 Reprographics &amp; Administration\n           \n      </span>\n    </span>\n    <span>\n      \n           - CLOSED\n          \n    </span>\n  </h3>\n  <h5>\n    <span>\n      \n           Part time - Monday to Friday - 9am to 3pm\n          \n    </span>\n  </h5>\n  <h5>\n    <span>\n      \n           \u014ctaki Campus\n          \n    </span>\n  </h5>\n</div>\n<div>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           Te W\u0101nanga o Raukawa is seeking a versatile and kaupapa-driven\u00a0\n          \n    </span>\n    <strong>\n      \n           Kaik\u014dkiri\u00a0\n          \n    </strong>\n    <span>\n      \n           to support both our reception and reprographic services. This part-time role involves a mix of front-of-house responsibilities and managing the production of printed materials. You\u2019ll be a key part of the daily rhythm of the W\u0101nanga\u2014welcoming manuhiri, supporting kaimahi and \u0101konga, and ensuring our resources are prepared to a high standard.\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <br />\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <strong>\n      \n           We\u2019re looking for someone who:\n          \n    </strong>\n  </p>\n  <ul>\n    <li>\n      <span>\n        \n            Welcomes others with aroha, confidence, and professionalism\n           \n      </span>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <span>\n        \n            Communicates clearly in both te reo M\u0101ori and English\n           \n      </span>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <span>\n        \n            Is organised, reliable, and detail-focused\n           \n      </span>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <span>\n        \n            Has experience with photocopying, printing, and related equipment\n           \n      </span>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <span>\n        \n            Upholds tikanga and the values of Te W\u0101nanga o Raukawa\n           \n      </span>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n      <span>\n        \n            Is committed to ongoing study and kaupapa M\u0101ori development\n           \n      </span>\n    </li>\n  </ul>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      <br />\n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <strong>\n      \n           Applications close on Wednesday 9\n          \n    </strong>\n    <sup>\n      <strong>\n        \n            th\n           \n      </strong>\n    </sup>\n    <strong>\n      \n           \u00a0of July 2025\n          \n    </strong>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <br />\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           For further information or to apply for this role, please contact:\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           \u00a0\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           Dionne Seng, Kaihaut\u016b Te Whare Tiaki Rawa\n          \n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      \n           \u012am\u0113ra:\u00a0\n          \n    </span>\n    <a href=\"mailto:dionne.seng@twor-otaki.ac.nz\" target=\"_blank\">\n      \n           dionne.seng@twor-otaki.ac.nz\n          \n    </a>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      <span>\n        \n            Waea: 06 3649011\n           \n      </span>\n    </span>\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <br />\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <span>\n      <br />\n    </span>\n  </p>\n</div>"
      }
    ],
